/surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Proximity of supermarkets is positively associated with diet quality index for pregnancy</article-title><source>Prev Med</source><volume>39</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>869</fpage><lpage>875</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15475018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ehp-117-442"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Larkin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Can cities be designed to fight obesity?</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>362</volume><issue>9389</issue><fpage>1046</fpage><lpage>1047</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14526776</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ehp-117-442"><citation citation-type="web"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Aiming to put more carts and better food on the streets </article-title><source>New York Times (New York City)</source><day>18</day><month>12</month><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2007/12/18/aiming-to-put-more-carts-and-better-food-on-the-streets/?scp=1&#x00026;sq=Aiming%20to%20put%20more%20carts%20and%20better%20food%20on%20the%20streets&#x00026;st=cse">http://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2007/12/18/aiming-to-put-more-carts-and-better-food-on-the-streets/?scp=1&#x00026;sq=Aiming%20to%20put%20more%20carts%20and%20better%20food%20on%20the%20streets&#x00026;st=cse</ext-link></comment><access-date>[accessed 3 February 2009]</access-date></citation></ref><ref id="b22-ehp-117-442"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>JS</given-na